        "original_id": "dc9b4eaf-ec46-591b-a117-6fdf58d6affb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Big Bad Wolf, Verbolten\n- Companies: Busch Gardens Williamsburg, Zierer\n- Places: Oktoberfest section, Williamsburg, Virginia, Germany\n- Concepts: suspended roller coaster, multi-launching steel roller coaster, soft opening\n\nFacts:\n- Big Bad Wolf was a suspended roller coaster in the Oktoberfest section of Busch Gardens Williamsburg.\n- Verbolten re-purposed the Big Bad Wolf footers, queue line, and station.\n- Verbolten began a soft opening at Busch Gardens Williamsburg in Williamsburg, Virginia on May 11, 2012.\n- Verbolten officially opened at Busch Gardens Williamsburg on May 18, 2012.\n- Verbolten is a Zierer multi-launching steel roller coaster.\n- The concept for Verbolten was jointly designed by the Busch Gardens Williamsburg creative design team and Zierer of Germany.\n- Verbolten was introduced in 2012.",
